    <string name="onb_nearby_title">Find phones around you</string>
    <string name="onb_nearby_body">The app needs to look for other phones and talk to them over Bluetooth.</string>
    <string name="onb_nearby_why_title">Why Android asks</string>
    <string name="onb_nearby_allow">Allow nearby devices</string>
    <string name="onb_nearby_ready">Everything is in place: the permissions are granted and Bluetooth is on.</string>
    <string name="onb_nearby_not_granted">The permission was not granted. Without it the app cannot find other phones. You can allow it now or later from the home screen.</string>
    <string name="onb_background_title">Staying connected</string>
    <string name="onb_background_body">To pass messages on while the screen is off, the app keeps running in the background.</string>
    <string name="onb_background_notification_title">A notification stays visible</string>
    <string name="onb_background_notification_body">Android shows a permanent notification while the app is connected. It shows how many neighbours are reachable and has a button to stop. That is how you can always tell the app is running.</string>
    <string name="onb_background_battery_title">Battery</string>
    <string name="onb_background_battery_body">Android may stop background apps to save power. Excluding this app from the battery optimisation keeps the mesh running with the screen off, at a small cost in battery. The power profile in the settings controls how much.</string>
    <string name="onb_battery_unrestricted">Not restricted: the app can keep running.</string>
    <string name="onb_battery_optimized">Optimised: Android may stop the app in the background.</string>
    <string name="onb_battery_open_settings">Open battery settings</string>
    <string name="onb_battery_oem_note">Some phone makers add their own limits (autostart, background activity). If the mesh stops when the screen turns off, allow background activity for this app in the phone’s settings.</string>
